# Decision tree

Agent routes from user intent **without requiring** a slash command unless the user wants the full skill ritual.

**Core routing:** [`change-control-manifest.mdc`](../change-control-manifest.mdc) § Skill orchestration (debug, builder-*, scrutinize, git-push, upgrade-ai, fix-record).

**Additional intents** (not repeated in manifest):

| User intent | First action |
|-------------|--------------|
| API / backend / REST | [`/builder-api`](../ai-skills/builder-api/SKILL.md) |
| deploy, CI/CD, IaC, observability | [`/builder-infrastructure`](../ai-skills/builder-infrastructure/SKILL.md) |
| mobile / native client bug | Debug discipline in **client repo** — not `/builder-feature` |
| durable vault memory | [`/vault-capture`](../ai-skills/vault-capture/SKILL.md) · recall [`/vault-recall`](../ai-skills/vault-recall/SKILL.md) |
| end-of-day triage / promote | [`/vault-daily`](../ai-skills/vault-daily/SKILL.md) — routine bullets via [`vault-autolog.mdc`](./vault-autolog.mdc) |
| one commit, multiple unrelated fixes | One fix-record per root cause — ask scope |
| unsure bug vs copy | One clarifying question, then manifest row |

**Active mode** (when multiple apply):

| Mode | Sequence |
|------|----------|
| Patch / fix (default) | diagnose → patch → verify → **vault autolog** ([manifest](../change-control-manifest.mdc) step 9) → optional capture/fix-record → git-push |
| Plan-only (`/builder-feature`) | plan → handoff — **no app patch** |
| Read-only (`/scrutinize`) | review → report — **no patch** until user approves |
| Meta upgrade (`/upgrade-ai`) | diagnose → minimal meta edit → verify — app sequence N/A |

Skill **iron law** overrides conflicting steps (plan-only, review-only, upgrade-ai on pack).
